{"version":1,"reference":{"kind":"artifact_content","namespace":"#1075","artifact_type":"_dh-work-item-head-v1","name":"head"},"owner_reference":"#1075","content":"{\"version\":1,\"issue_reference\":\"#1075\",\"parent_revision\":\"b471e5966106f89a74b6a0afbc1a5252e15a3c1c75ba3d23c5ca5db4f878f907\",\"root_revision\":\"b471e5966106f89a74b6a0afbc1a5252e15a3c1c75ba3d23c5ca5db4f878f907\",\"body\":\"<!-- backlog-metadata:\\npriority: P1\\ntype: Feature\\nstatus: open\\nadded: 2026-08-12\\n-->\\n\\n## Description\\n\\nAdd stable semantic node IDs to the 9 Mermaid flowcharts in backlog-item-lifecycle.md and define input/output/edge contracts per node. This enables orchestrators to dispatch agents by node reference rather than prose prompts. Each node gets: a stable ID (e.g., P2_RTICA_FINAL), input contract (what artifacts/data must be available), output contract (what the node produces and where it persists), edge conditions (observable facts determining the next node), and actor (who executes). Skills reference their entry/exit nodes instead of re-describing context. The lifecycle doc becomes a process contract, not just documentation. Backend storage primitives (IssueBackend, DocumentBackend, TaskBackend) provide the vocabulary for output types.\\n\\n## RT-ICA\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nRT-ICA Snapshot: Lifecycle document node contracts \u2014 stable IDs with input/output/edge specifications per node\\nDate: 2026-04-23\\nGoal: Add stable semantic node IDs and formal input/output/edge contracts to the Mermaid flowcharts in backlog-item-lifecycle.md.\\n\\nConditions:\\n1. backlog-item-lifecycle.md location | AVAILABLE | plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md\\n2. Number of Mermaid flowcharts | DERIVABLE | description says 9 (needs re-count after any recent doc changes)\\n3. Backend storage primitive vocabulary | AVAILABLE | IssueBackend, DocumentBackend, TaskBackend defined in backend_protocol.py and task_backend.py\\n4. Node ID convention | AVAILABLE (documented) | format: {Phase}_{NodeName}_FINAL e.g. P2_RTICA_FINAL \u2014 from description\\n5. Contract format per node | AVAILABLE (documented) | input contract, output contract, edge conditions, actor\\n6. Consumer skills that would reference node IDs | DERIVABLE | groom-backlog-item, work-backlog-item, rt-ica skill, feature-researcher \u2014 needs audit of which skills reference lifecycle stages\\n\\nAVAILABLE count: 4\\nDERIVABLE count: 2\\nMISSING count: 0\\n\\nDecision: APPROVED \u2014 documentation change; no code changes required. Consumer skill updates are a follow-on (not in scope of this item).\\n</div>\\n\\n## Groomed (2026-04-23)\\n\\n### Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n- [ ] Every Mermaid flowchart node in `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` has a stable semantic ID (format: `{Phase}_{NodeName}`, e.g. `P2_RTICA_FINAL`)\\n- [ ] Each node has an associated contract block in the document: input contract (artifacts/data required), output contract (what is produced and where), edge conditions (observable facts for each outgoing edge), actor (which agent or human executes)\\n- [ ] IssueBackend, DocumentBackend, TaskBackend are used as the vocabulary for output contract types\\n- [ ] `grep -c 'P2_RTICA' plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` returns non-zero (spot check that node IDs are present)\\n- [ ] `uv run prek run --files plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` passes (markdown linting)\\n- [ ] At least one consuming skill (e.g. `groom-backlog-item`) is updated to reference entry/exit node IDs rather than re-describing the stage context\\n\\n### Files\\n\\n- `plugins/development-harness/docs/backlog-item-lifecycle.md` \u2014 primary change (add node IDs + contracts)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/backlog_core/backend_protocol.py` \u2014 IssueBackend vocabulary (read-only reference)\\n- `plugins/development-harness/sam_schema/core/task_backend.py` \u2014 TaskBackend vocabulary (read-only reference)\\n- One or more skill SKILL.md files in `plugins/development-harness/skills/` \u2014 update to reference node IDs (TBD which skills after lifecycle audit)\\n\\n### Story\\n\\nAs an **orchestrator dispatching agents at specific lifecycle stage transitions**, I want **stable node IDs with input/output/edge contracts in `backlog-item-lifecycle.md`** so that **I can reference nodes by ID and know exactly what artifacts must be present before entering a node and what will be produced when it exits**.\\n\\n## Story\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\nAs a **developer using Claude Code skills**, I want to **lifecycle document node contracts \u2014 stable ids with input/output/edge specifications per node** so that **the tooling becomes more capable and complete**.\\n</div>\\n\\n## Acceptance Criteria\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- [ ] Work matches description\\n- [ ] Plan or implementation complete\\n</div>\\n\\n## Context\\n\\n<div><sub>0000-00-00T00:00:00Z</sub>\\n\\n- **Source**: Session observation \u2014 lifecycle doc triage + user design direction\\n- **Priority**: P1\\n- **Added**: 2026-03-25\\n- **Research questions**: None\\n</div>\\n\",\"digest\":\"18e1dfac6ddb6f72dfa33ba55eb4b7746e3b9472b8742f2ec24170b46201661e\",\"comment_id\":\"IC_kwDOQGimCs8AAAABPS78pQ\"}"}